From 43192ebddac82c303d27df690283b9a2f31094c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:52:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bootwait: 9-line X68000 Z banner; elapsed seconds from the
 Pico's clock; next-retry countdown
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- The banner is now a framed 7-row block font (9 lines, plain ASCII, no
  backslash). Rows: banner 2-10, subtitle 11, title 13, status 15,
  animation 17, keys 19-20.
- On the Z the seconds were reported counting down. The waiter no longer
  uses IOCS _ONTIME for the number: it shows "経過 N 秒" from the
  difference of the Pico's uptime in the replies (+12), which only goes
  up. _ONTIME is still used for pacing and the poll slot, now with the
  absolute difference, so a clock running backwards still polls every
  0.5 s at fresh slots.
- The reply carries the time until the Pico's next connection attempt
  (+24; connect.c keeps connect_next_ms): "(次の再接続まで N 秒)", or
  "(接続を試しています)" during an attempt; nothing once connected.
- waiter_test.py: banner lines from art.txt, seconds count up, retry
  texts, a backwards ONTIME.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PrGdt1XK1exBgERrMmLA1u
